prim<m:=(v,v,v)> between_exclusive(x, left, right):
  brief_description "Tests whether each lane of x lies in the exclusive range left < x < right."
  detailed_description """
    Checks each lane of `x` against the exclusive range bounded by `left` and
    `right`, returning a mask for lanes where `left < x < right`. Signedness
    follows the selected lane type, and floating-point unordered cases follow
    the selected backend comparison predicates.
